window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-acc8cb67be71d07d"]={"zh":"<h1 id=\"composer-predictions\">下一条消息预测（Composer Predictions）</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 后添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>Composer predictions（消息预测）会在 Codex 桌面应用中为你的下一条消息提供自动补全式建议。Codex 回复后，它会根据当前对话，在消息输入框中建议一条后续提示词。按 <strong>Tab</strong> 可将建议的消息接受为可编辑草稿，也可以直接输入自己的消息。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图说明：Codex 回复后，消息输入框中出现一条预测建议；按 Tab 可将其作为草稿接受，但不会立即发送。</p> </blockquote> <p>要使用消息预测，请确保已更新 <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11369540-using-codex-with-your-chatgpt-plan\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Codex 桌面应用（需联网）</a>，并使用你的个人 ChatGPT Pro 账户登录。</p> <p><a id=\"tab-to-accept\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"tab\">按 Tab 接受建议</h2> <ol> <li>在受支持的线程中发送消息。Codex 回复完成后，查看消息输入框中是否出现建议。</li> <li><strong>按 Tab 接受预测。</strong> 建议文本会成为输入框中的可编辑草稿。</li> <li>检查文本并按需修改，准备好后再发送。</li> </ol> <p>如果你想写别的内容，可以直接开始输入自己的消息，不必等待预测。接受预测只会把文字填入消息输入框，不会替你发送消息。</p> <p><a id=\"how-predictions-use-context\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">预测如何使用上下文</h2> <p>预测会使用当前线程中的对话。如果线程里已经包含过去工作的上下文或已连接应用的信息，这些内容可能影响预测。预测功能本身不会主动查找记忆，也不会自行从已连接的应用中检索信息。</p> <p>如果你启用了记忆，线程中已有的记忆上下文可能让预测更贴合你的情况。关闭记忆时也可以使用预测功能。</p> <p><a id=\"availability-and-controls\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">可用范围与控制</h2> <p>消息预测目前处于 Beta 测试阶段，面向年满 18 岁、使用个人 ChatGPT Pro 方案且所在地区受支持的用户。它可在 Codex 桌面应用的本地线程和 SSH 线程中使用，支持的模型包括 GPT-6 Astra 和 GPT-6.1 Sol。符合条件的用户默认启用预测。你可以在 <strong>Settings（设置）→ General（常规）→ Composer（撰写器）</strong> 中，通过 <strong>Show predictions（显示预测）</strong> 开关启用或关闭。</p> <p>生成预测不会计入 Codex 用量限制，也不会消耗额度。发送消息时（包括发送已接受的预测内容），仍会按正常规则计算 Codex 用量并计费。</p> <p>如需了解设置和故障排查，请参阅 <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001601-composer-predictions-in-codex\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Codex 中的 Composer predictions（需联网）</a>。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"composer-predictions\">Composer Predictions</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Composer predictions provides autocomplete-style suggestions for your next message in the Codex desktop app. After Codex responds, it uses the current conversation to suggest a follow-up prompt in the message box. Press <strong>Tab</strong> to accept the suggested message as an editable draft, or type your own message.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: Codex responds, a prediction appears in the message box, and pressing Tab accepts it as a draft without sending it.</p> </blockquote> <p>To use composer predictions, make sure you've updated the <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11369540-using-codex-with-your-chatgpt-plan\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Codex desktop app (online)</a> and have signed in to your personal ChatGPT Pro account.</p> <h2 id=\"tab-to-accept\">Tab to accept</h2> <ol> <li>Send a message in a supported thread. When Codex finishes responding, look for a suggestion in the message box.</li> <li><strong>Press Tab to accept the prediction.</strong> The suggested text becomes an editable draft in the message box.</li> <li>Review the text, make any changes, then send it when you’re ready.</li> </ol> <p>To write something else, start typing your own message. You can keep typing without waiting for a prediction. Accepting a prediction adds text to the message box. It does not send the message for you.</p> <h2 id=\"how-predictions-use-context\">How predictions use context</h2> <p>Predictions use the conversation in your current thread. If context from past work or connected apps is already in that thread, it can inform a prediction. Predictions don’t look up memories or retrieve information from connected apps on their own. If you have memory enabled, memory context already in your thread can personalize predictions. You can use predictions with memory off.</p> <h2 id=\"availability-and-controls\">Availability and controls</h2> <p>Composer predictions is currently in beta for users aged 18 and older on personal ChatGPT Pro plans in supported regions. It’s available in local and SSH threads in the Codex desktop app with GPT-6 Astra and GPT-6.1 Sol. Predictions are enabled by default for eligible users. You can turn them on or off using the <strong>Show predictions</strong> toggle in <strong>Settings → General → Composer</strong>.</p> <p>Generating predictions doesn’t count toward your Codex usage limits or consume credits. When you send a message, including an accepted prediction, normal Codex usage limits and billing apply.</p> <p>For setup and troubleshooting, see <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001601-composer-predictions-in-codex\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Composer predictions in Codex (online)</a>.</p>"};
